<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kuban Rada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1917–1920</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Kuban Legislative Rada</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kuban <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radaa">Rada</a> was the elected assembly and regional government of the Kuban <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a>, formed after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/february-revolution">February Revolution</a> of 1917. It declared the Kuban an autonomous and then an independent people's republic, allied uneasily with the White <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volunteer-army">Volunteer Army</a> against the Bolsheviks and sought ties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>. It was dissolved when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> conquered the Kuban in 1920.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kuban-rada.jpg" alt="Kuban Rada" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alex Tora · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Herb_Kubanskoyi_Narodnoyi_Respubliky.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
